# Text files are stored with LF and checked out as the platform prefers,
# except shell scripts: bash cannot run a script with CRLF line endings, which
# is what Git for Windows would otherwise give scripts/backup.sh and restore.sh.
# Windows batch files the other way: cmd can misread labels in LF ones.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
